
  ✖ skip-added  Test skipped
    error · tests

  New skip/disable markers (`it.skip`, `xit`, `@pytest.mark.skip`, `t.Skip`, `#[ignore]`,
  `@Disabled`).

  A skipped test cannot fail, so skipping a failing test hides the bug instead of fixing it.

  Bad:

  │ it.skip('rejects expired tokens', async () => {
  │   expect(await verify(expired)).toBe(false)
  │ })

  Good: fix `verify()` so the test passes. narc recognizes:

  • `it.skip`, `describe.skip`, `xit`, `xdescribe` (Jest, Vitest, Mocha)
  • `@pytest.mark.skip` and `pytest.skip()` (pytest)
  • `t.Skip()` (Go), `#[ignore]` (Rust), `@Disabled` (JUnit)

  See the waiver guide (https://github.com/huyth45/narc#waivers) when a skip is really intended.

  How to fix
    Fix the code under test so the test passes instead of skipping it. If the test itself is wrong,
    fix the test and say why in the commit.

  If the change is intentional
    Waive it with a reason, in a comment on the flagged line or the line above:
      // narc:allow skip-added reason="<why this is fine>"
    or for whole paths, in .narc.yml:
      allow:
        - rule: skip-added
          path: "src/legacy/**"
          reason: "<why this is fine>"

  Docs: https://github.com/huyth45/narc/blob/main/docs/rules.md#skip-added

